  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b1_u03_l1_g1",
      "pattern": "저는 N이에요/예요",
      "meaning_uz": "Men ...man: o'zini tanishtirish",
      "meaning_en": "I am N: introducing yourself",
      "explanation_md": "**N이에요/예요** — \"... (dir)\" degan ma'noni beradi. O'zingizni tanishtirganda **저는** (\"men\") bilan boshlaysiz.\n\n**저는 아지즈예요.** — *Men Azizman.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n- Ot **받침 bilan tugasa** → **-이에요**: 학생 → **학생이에요**, 사람 → **사람이에요**\n- Ot **unli bilan tugasa** → **-예요**: 아지즈 → **아지즈예요**, 의사 → **의사예요**\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- **저** — \"men\"ning kamtarona shakli. Notanish odam bilan doim **저** deng.\n- **-는** — mavzu qo'shimchasi: **저는** = \"men esam / menga kelsak\".\n- Fe'l doim **gap oxirida** keladi, xuddi o'zbekchadagidek.",
      "explanation_md_en": "**N이에요/예요** means \"(I) am / (it) is N\". To introduce yourself, start with **저는** (\"I\").\n\n**저는 아지즈예요.** — *I'm Aziz.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n- Noun **ends in 받침** → **-이에요**: 학생 → **학생이에요**, 사람 → **사람이에요**\n- Noun **ends in a vowel** → **-예요**: 아지즈 → **아지즈예요**, 의사 → **의사예요**\n\n### Remember\n\n- **저** is the humble \"I\". Use it with people you don't know well.\n- **-는** marks the topic: **저는** = \"as for me\".\n- The verb always comes **at the end** of the sentence.",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 bor",
          "condition_en": "With 받침",
          "rule": "N + 이에요",
          "example": "학생 → 학생이에요, 사람 → 사람이에요"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 yo'q",
          "condition_en": "No 받침",
          "rule": "N + 예요",
          "example": "아지즈 → 아지즈예요, 의사 → 의사예요"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "저는 아지즈예요.",
          "uz": "Men Azizman.",
          "en": "I'm Aziz.",
          "audio": "1e619efde032.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "저는 우즈베키스탄 사람이에요.",
          "uz": "Men o'zbekistonlikman.",
          "en": "I'm from Uzbekistan.",
          "audio": "08c19379f27c.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "저는 민지예요.",
          "uz": "Men Minjiman.",
          "en": "I'm Minji.",
          "audio": "20feb86b1832.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "저는 한국 사람이에요.",
          "uz": "Men koreysman.",
          "en": "I'm Korean.",
          "audio": "a8ef97852560.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "제 고향은 사마르칸트예요.",
          "uz": "Mening ona shahrim — Samarqand.",
          "en": "My hometown is Samarkand.",
          "audio": "4e5ed98823d8.mp3"
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "저는 학생예요.",
          "right": "저는 학생이에요.",
          "why_uz": "학생 받침 bilan tugaydi (ㅇ), shuning uchun -이에요.",
          "why_en": "학생 ends in 받침 (ㅇ), so it takes -이에요."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "저는 아지즈이에요.",
          "right": "저는 아지즈예요.",
          "why_uz": "아지즈 unli bilan tugaydi, shuning uchun -예요.",
          "why_en": "아지즈 ends in a vowel, so it takes -예요."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "나는 미국 사람이에요.",
          "right": "저는 미국 사람이에요.",
          "why_uz": "Tanishuvda kamtarona 저 ishlatiladi.",
          "why_en": "When meeting someone, use the humble 저."
        }
      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchada 'Men Azizman' deymiz: '-man' qo'shimchasi otga qo'shiladi. Koreyschada ham shunday: 아지즈 + 예요. Faqat koreyschada qo'shimcha shaxsga qarab o'zgarmaydi: 'men talabaman', 'u talaba' — ikkalasi ham 학생이에요.",
      "compare_en": "In English you say 'I am Aziz' with a separate verb 'am'. In Korean the 'am/is/are' part is an ending on the noun: 아지즈 + 예요. It never changes for the person: 'I am a student' and 'she is a student' are both 학생이에요."
    },
    {
      "id": "b1_u03_l1_g2",
      "pattern": "N이에요/예요?",
      "meaning_uz": "...mi?: so'roq gap",
      "meaning_en": "Is it N?: asking a question",
      "explanation_md": "So'roq gap yasash uchun **N이에요/예요** gapining oxirida ovozni **ko'taring** va yozuvda **?** qo'ying. So'z tartibi o'zgarmaydi.\n\n**아지즈 씨는 학생이에요?** — *Aziz, siz talabamisiz?*\n\n### Javob berish\n\n- **네, 학생이에요.** — *Ha, talabaman.*\n- **아니요, 선생님이에요.** — *Yo'q, o'qituvchiman.*\n\n### \"Qaysi\" va \"nima\" so'roq so'zlari\n\n- **어느 나라 사람이에요?** — *Qaysi mamlakatdansiz?*\n- **이름이 뭐예요?** — *Ismingiz nima?* (뭐 + 예요)\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Suhbatdoshga **당신** (\"siz\") demang — bu qo'pol eshitiladi. Uning ismini **씨** bilan ayting: **민지 씨는 …?**",
      "explanation_md_en": "To make a question, keep **N이에요/예요** and **raise your voice** at the end; in writing add **?**. The word order does not change.\n\n**아지즈 씨는 학생이에요?** — *Aziz, are you a student?*\n\n### Answering\n\n- **네, 학생이에요.** — *Yes, I am.*\n- **아니요, 선생님이에요.** — *No, I'm a teacher.*\n\n### \"Which\" and \"what\"\n\n- **어느 나라 사람이에요?** — *Which country are you from?*\n- **이름이 뭐예요?** — *What's your name?* (뭐 + 예요)\n\n### Remember\n\n- Don't call someone **당신** (\"you\") — it sounds rude. Use their name with **씨**: **민지 씨는 …?**",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 bor",
          "condition_en": "With 받침",
          "rule": "N + 이에요?",
          "example": "학생 → 학생이에요?"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "받침 yo'q",
          "condition_en": "No 받침",
          "rule": "N + 예요?",
          "example": "뭐 → 뭐예요?, 의사 → 의사예요?"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "어느 나라 사람이에요?",
          "uz": "Qaysi mamlakatdansiz?",
          "en": "Which country are you from?",
          "audio": "459469d4fef0.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "이름이 뭐예요?",
          "uz": "Ismingiz nima?",
          "en": "What's your name?",
          "audio": "26609ee489e1.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "민지 씨는 한국 사람이에요?",
          "uz": "Minji, siz koreysmisiz?",
          "en": "Minji, are you Korean?",
          "audio": "ace8e2bf90eb.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "네, 한국 사람이에요.",
          "uz": "Ha, koreysman.",
          "en": "Yes, I'm Korean.",
          "audio": "fff10d5946b8.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "고향이 어디예요?",
          "uz": "Ona shahringiz qayer?",
          "en": "Where is your hometown?",
          "audio": "5227d4b21055.mp3"
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "이름이 뭐이에요?",
          "right": "이름이 뭐예요?",
          "why_uz": "뭐 unli bilan tugaydi: 뭐예요.",
          "why_en": "뭐 ends in a vowel: 뭐예요."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "어느 나라 사람예요?",
          "right": "어느 나라 사람이에요?",
          "why_uz": "사람 받침 bilan tugaydi: 사람이에요.",
          "why_en": "사람 ends in 받침: 사람이에요."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "당신은 학생이에요?",
          "right": "민지 씨는 학생이에요?",
          "why_uz": "당신 qo'pol eshitiladi; ism + 씨 ishlating.",
          "why_en": "당신 sounds rude; use the name + 씨."
        }
      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchada so'roq uchun '-mi' qo'shamiz: 'talabaMIsiz?'. Koreyschada qo'shimcha qo'shilmaydi — faqat ovoz ko'tariladi: 학생이에요 → 학생이에요?",
      "compare_en": "In English you swap the words to ask: 'You are' → 'Are you?'. In Korean nothing moves: you just raise your voice at the end: 학생이에요 → 학생이에요?"
    }
